    "body": "fix on issue/3514-motion-slow-tests-a · PR #3726 · pinned by the six `_light` twins in `crates/motion/src/machining2d/adaptive_troch_heavy_tests.rs` · merges when reviewed\n\nThis PR is slice A only. It says `Refs #3514`, so it does not close the issue. These tests remain:\n\n- Slice B, `crates/motion/src/machining2d/adaptive/tests.rs`:\n  - `the_slot_and_its_32_nm_twin_decide_the_same_way`\n  - `a_channel_is_grown_as_one_spiral_that_never_crosses`\n- Slice B, `crates/motion/src/machining2d/pocket_hsm_ring.rs`:\n  - `an_air_plan_over_the_load_bound_is_refused_by_name`\n- Slice C, `crates/motion/tests/adaptive_troch_neck.rs`:\n  - `triangle_and_wide_to_narrow_neck_are_cleared`\n- Slice C, `crates/motion/tests/adaptive_troch_island.rs`:\n  - `pocket_with_island_is_cleared_without_crossing_or_excess_rest`\n  - `ring_round_island_is_cleared_with_closed_lane`\n- Slice C, `crates/motion/tests/adaptive_troch_parallel.rs`:\n  - `corner_cleanup_reduces_34x16_rest_to_at_most_hsm_rest`\n\nFinding: the debug times of #3427 come from a parallel run of the whole crate. `without_lift_room_the_returns_retract_and_a_plunge_entry_is_said_unread` alone takes 14.7 s in debug, not 72.5 s. Measure the remaining tests alone in debug before each slice. A test under 60 s alone can stay in the default suite.\n",
